Lexifina's own contributions to this repository (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the
folder layout, the tables and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

The legal texts are not Lexifina's. They come from:

1. Botswana e-Laws, https://elaws.gov.bw, published by the Attorney General's Chambers of Botswana. Footer:
   "Copyright (c) 2026. AGC, Botswana All rights reserved." Disclaimer (https://elaws.gov.bw/disclaimer): the
   materials are "provided by the Government for information purposes only"; the electronic versions "are not
   recognized as the official or authorized version"; authorised printed copies are available from the Department
   of Printing and Publishing Services.

2. botswanalaws.com, the earlier site of the same consolidation (published for the Attorney General's Chambers by
   Blackhall Publishing), read only from archived copies on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org):
   the Constitution captured 2019-05-26 and the Penal Code captured 2024-12-04. Notice: "Copyright (c) 2026.
   All right reserved. Government of Botswana."

The Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act (Cap. 68:02) of Botswana, section 6(2)(b), provides that no protection
extends under the Act to "any official text of a legislative, administrative or legal nature, as well as any
official translation thereof" (text as published on Botswana e-Laws,
https://elaws.gov.bw/principal-legislation/copyright-and-neighbouring-rights/).

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per section or schedule, one paragraph
per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; amendment and editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were
left out; and the versions were arranged as dated git commits. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the
Government of Botswana nor Blackhall Publishing endorses this repository.
